## Key Stakeholders

![Team](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1522071820081-009f0129c71c?w=1200)

Successful AI deployment is collaborative, involving diverse roles.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    PM["Product Manager"] --> DS["Data Scientist / ML Engineer"]
    DS --> SW["Software Engineer"]
    SW --> OPS["DevOps / MLOps"]
    QA["QA Engineer"] --> OPS
    USERS["End Users"] --> DS
    USERS --> PM
    OPS --> USERS
```

### 1. Data Scientists / ML Engineers

- **Role:** Design, develop, train, and evaluate AI models.
- **Responsibilities:** Model development, algorithm selection, performance optimization, preparing artifacts, collaborating on integration, monitoring production performance.
- **Example:** Dr. Anya Sharma develops a deep learning model for medical image analysis and provides the trained TensorFlow SavedModel to the deployment team.

### 2. Software Engineers / Backend Developers

- **Role:** Build applications and services hosting the AI model.
- **Responsibilities:** API development (FastAPI), model integration, data pipelines, robust infrastructure, user interfaces.
- **Example:** Ben Carter builds a REST API using FastAPI that sends queries to Dr. Sharma's model and returns diagnostic suggestions.

### 3. DevOps / MLOps Engineers

- **Role:** Bridge development and operations; automate deployment, management, monitoring.
- **Responsibilities:** CI/CD pipelines, containerization (Docker), orchestration (Kubernetes), cloud infrastructure, monitoring/logging, reproducibility, automated retraining.
- **Example:** Maria Rodriguez sets up a CI/CD pipeline that builds Docker images on model commit, configures Kubernetes for scaling, and sets up Prometheus/Grafana monitoring.

### 4. Product Managers

- **Role:** Define vision, strategy, and roadmap for AI products.
- **Responsibilities:** Business problem definition, feature prioritization, requirements translation, stakeholder management, alignment with business goals, release decisions.
- **Example:** David Lee identifies the need for an AI diagnostic tool for radiologists, defines features and timelines with the team.

### 5. Quality Assurance (QA) Engineers

- **Role:** Ensure overall quality, functionality, and reliability.
- **Responsibilities:** Test plans and cases, bug tracking, functional/performance/regression/UAT testing, validating model outputs, ensuring requirements are met.
- **Example:** Sarah Chen designs test cases verifying the AI correctly identifies diseases and the UI handles errors gracefully.

### 6. Business Stakeholders / End-Users

- **Role:** Ultimate users and beneficiaries of the AI system.
- **Responsibilities:** Domain expertise, UAT participation, feedback, adoption.
- **Example:** Radiologists provide feedback on the accuracy and usefulness of AI diagnostic suggestions.

